WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.480
This story began with a chance
train encounter on New Year's Eve.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.543
Santa Claus was
going home from the war.

00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:55.695
I've come from serious places,
where there's combat,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:02.400
to visit the kids
and wish them a Happy New Year.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.400
For myself, I'd wish...

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:11.400
probably for peace to begin
and for this war to end.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.360
- I'll be in touch!
- Send it to me, OK?

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.680
Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.280
His name was llya.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.240
To my surprise, llya turned out to be
a Ukrainian fighting on Russia's side.

00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:31.573
We exchanged numbers
and agreed to be in touch.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.480
Happy New Year, Moscow!-

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.480
Glory to Heroes of Russia! -

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.720
I didn't expect this war.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.800
I thought that after losing so many lives to conflict,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.920
we Russians would finally find our wars consigned to history.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.360
But it's almost a year
since Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.320
Almost a year since the shock
of waking as citizens of a warring state.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.840
And today, my compatriots in uniform
look on from these posters.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.760
Who are these guys?

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.840
In Russian media, they're heroes
who always win and never die.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.360
In the West, they're war criminals,
reigning terror and destruction.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:31.680
The fog of war is so thick you barely
see the human stories it's made of.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:51.600
llya's story, a Ukrainian in Russian
uniform, was the first thread I could pull.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.840
- I'm waiting!
And l'll return!

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.120
Promise?
- I promise.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.360
Alive, most importantly...

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.200
Alive, of course, baby.
- And not wounded!

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.600
- Alive, of course, baby.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:06.600
And not wounded!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.600
I'll try not to get wounded.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.800
Once more!
Not over the doorstep.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.320
In 200 metres, turn right.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.400
For me, the war didn't start in 2022.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.360
It started in 2014.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.640
That was the beginning
of the civil war, roughly speaking, in Ukraine.

00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:59.120
I lost my home, I lost my business.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.120
Basically, they took it all.

00:05:04.927 --> 00:05:08.599
That was when
I parted ways with Ukraine.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.640
- Kiev Railway Station, Moscow -

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.680
All will be well.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.000
We just have to fight a bit more.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.640
I didn't fully understand llya's story then.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.560
But when he called from the front,
I begged to join him.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.720
I'm here completely unofficially.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.355
I'm going at my own risk, of course.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.120
Without Defence Ministry permission.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:09.960
Without Defence Ministry permission

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.480
Not even press accreditation.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.680
I'm interested...

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.240
It's no idle interest, but an attempt
to understand what's going on...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.600
With my country.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:43.987
bridge inscription: Dedicated to the
Eternal Russian-Ukrainian Friendship -

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.800
This is the 'Lugansk People's Republic.'

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.240
This is the 'Lugansk People's Republic.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.800
Or 'occupied Eastern Ukraine.'

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.680
Or 'new Russian territories.'

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.920
It depends who you ask.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.271
I was sure l'd be sent back,
maybe even arrested.

00:07:08.856 --> 00:07:10.812
But trying isn't torture.

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:17.436
I introduced myself to the command,
and said I'm making a documentary,

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:24.245
about different fates in this war and
I was interested in filming some soldiers.

00:07:24.848 --> 00:07:30.240
Well, first they allowed it, then forbade it,
then allowed it again, then...

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.600
...well, it's not clear.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.400
The battalion's in the rear temporarily,
180km from the front.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:51.120
For now, the supply unit
has adopted me.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.840
Here's a uniform for you too.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.280
There's nothing smaller.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:02.400
They gave me a sleeping bag, boots
and a uniform so I wouldn't stand out.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.240
Whose house is this?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.760
It was offered to us by a local granny.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:20.520
She doesn't live here.
Well, she tends to the garden.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.400
So they just gave you the house?

00:08:24.695 --> 00:08:28.784
Yes. So you could say
we're having a nice rest here.

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:38.771
We don't have many personnel
left from previous battles...

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:45.480
so now they're adding new people.

00:08:50.945 --> 00:08:55.560
As soon as the unit's replenished,
back to the front.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.800
Several battalions are stationed
temporarily in this village.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.320
Anastasia, they're here.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.800
The guys are taking food
to friends coming from the front.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.360
Anastasia, this is the 1st battalion,
what's left of it.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.800
Out of 900, only 300 remain, right?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.763
- Honestly, I don't even remember.
- You don't remember?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.960
The survivors are left.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.880
As they say...

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.520
we are ill-fated.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.400
We...

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.880
I'll just get my brains together.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.160
I have!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.600
- They dumped us there.
- We were dumped and got surrounded.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:04.320
We didn't know how to get out of there.
We took the first fire fight, just a bit...

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.114
Just a bit.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.600
There! I even have tears. Fuck.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:16.920
To be honest, we were
attacked pretty fucking badly.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.520
How
of us came back?
many

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.520
Out of 900, just 300 people.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.240
Half of them are crippled.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.560
And in these seven months...

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:43.708
Oh, fuck! I forgot to tell
someone stole my left brain hemisphere.

00:10:43.825 --> 00:10:47.160
We searched all night but didn't find it.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:53.400
I was told at the hospital that
my left brain hemisphere was stolen.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:57.840
Because of that, my left arm
doesn't work, and my left leg limps.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.120
Do you have family? Kids?

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:06.120
No, I'm divorced.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.840
And what is our fate?

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:11.760
No family.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.600
Kids? Well, there are,
but you can say, not.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.480
My contract ended on February 7th.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.800
All of ours on the 7th.
His in January, can you believe it?

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:26.880
What can you do? Fuck all!

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:31.021
What do they tell you?
To the trenches!

00:11:31.173 --> 00:11:34.158
Go back?
They want to send you back?

00:11:34.185 --> 00:11:36.827
- Are you able to go back?
-No.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.000
Anastasia, what are you filming?
- A documentary.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:45.000
It's about us. With the truth.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.480
Not like on TV, but the truth.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.600
- Star: equips you with knowledge

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:55.200
Anastasia, never believe
what they show on TV.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.400
They don't just lie, they bullshit.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.840
llya's battalion has only 80 people left out of 400.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:35.280
To make up for losses, 300 'newbies' were added.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.720
Most were drafted,
and have no military experience.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:44.520
was surprised that some
followed someone voluntarily,

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:47.760
a father with a son,
or a friend with a friend.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.760
Smarty, bring everyone here.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:52.680
We're coming!

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.440
Wait, we're warming up.
OK, let's go.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.000
Who's shooting?

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:58.680
Over here.

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:02.400
They're already loaded.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.960
20 people willing to shoot.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.560
20 people who want to shoot.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:11.760
CMBHAR

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:11.880
BOAK

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.200
When you're above,
controlling the drone,

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:36.480
you look at all the people,
they're so small. Defenceless.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.760
lam the eyes and ears of my comrades.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.280
My callsign is Cap.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:53.400
I'm here because I followed
my friend voluntarily, I wasn't drafted.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.920
He's just, 'Cartoon'.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:01.440
He and I, we're like,
best friends since childhood.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:05.400
Before the draft,
I didn't think about it at all.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.400
Then, when my call-up came through,

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:12.720
I kind of sat, thought about it,
and decided that I had to go.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.000
After all, my family...

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:18.960
I want them all to be alive and well.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:22.440
What's the threat to your family?
What do you fight for?

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:24.720
Nazism!

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:27.840
Most of all, Nazism. I hate it.

00:14:28.282 --> 00:14:29.583
Because...

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:33.720
People, they're all the same.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.960
It doesn't matter what nation,

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:40.560
or what religion, we're all people!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.520
And then there are Nazis.
I just hate them.

00:14:46.987 --> 00:14:50.400
- You think there's a lot here in Ukraine?
- Yes.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.440
Here, the majority of
Ukrainian people hate Russians.

00:14:55.997 --> 00:14:57.960
But why, I just can't understand.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.640
How do you know they hate Russians?

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.480
Well, from the fact that the war started.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:29.520
First of all, I came here
to fight for my friend, Cartoon.

00:15:30.693 --> 00:15:35.373
And secondly, I want
revenge for my dead comrades

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.440
Three classmates died.

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:46.320
Of course, it's bad, but I want revenge.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.840
- Vitaly, do we light a fire?

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:14.880
Unlike the newly drafted, the supply unit
is almost entirely volunteers.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:22.680
I don't know about you, but I fight
for my women. So they live well.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:24.600
Fucking bullshit.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:28.200
You're 50, alone,
and have nothing, damn it.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.720
You're not here for a woman.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.120
Then for whom?
- For yourself.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.280
To profit and to shit.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.760
Fuck!
For sluts and alcohol.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:42.840
Vitaly!

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:48.240
I've been here for eight months, bro.
Eight months.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:49.800
So?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.560
It's a shame you don't have a woman.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.160
Yuri, I had a woman. I've told you.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:59.160
She said I won't go back,
that I'd be killed.
179
00:16:58,800 --&gt; 00:16:58,320
that l'd be killed.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.240
She said. I won't go back,

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:02.880
That was it, we broke up.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:06.600
I left her a two-bedroom flat!
For her kid.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:08.880
Fuck me!

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:12.480
I'm very happy that
there are people like you!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.960
I'm not like that, and so what?

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.600
Yura, you're an old fool.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.760
Because your women are golddiggers.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.160
But they text me.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:32.400
You're not here for Russia or patriotism
but for money, so you can waste it later.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.760
Yes, exactly that, Vitaly.
- Well, it's dumb.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.810
And why are you here?
- Me?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.680
I told you why I'm here.

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:42.360
Once again.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.000
I came here for patriotism.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:47.280
Do you see it?

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.560
Not anymore, unfortunately.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:52.200
I'm so sorry for you, Vitaly.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:55.800
Because, in that, you're not alone here.

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.280
You're not alone here, Vitaly.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:08.640
OK, where's the moonshine?

00:18:09.347 --> 00:18:10.667
You say 'gorilka', right?

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.840
Gorilka, gorilka.
- In Ukrainian.
203
00:18:12,865 --&gt; 00:18:12,240
- Gorilka, gorilka.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:15.720
Pour it on the table.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:20.520
There, it's burning already.
- I don't like that smell.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.800
I'm already drunk.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:29.520
First of all, I want to drink
to the boys fighting here with us.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:32.520
Those who are here.

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:36.360
And those who will join us.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:47.400
As for the war,
what are we fighting for here?

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:50.520
I'll tell you simply...

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.000
Here, everyone has the same motive.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:00.360
Say 'money' and I'll kill you.

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.400
Money!

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:06.600
Money 100%. It's 100% money. But!

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:08.280
You're wrong.
- But! But...

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:11.880
Why deny that we all have
our own motivation?

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:14.760
Why impose that one?

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:18.240
I don't get you 50-year-old men,

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.800
who only think about
money, money, money!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.800
Where will you take it all, to your grave?

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.800
Is money really the most important thing?

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.840
Of course it's not!

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:35.640
You have no one to feed.
You don't have shit, so you talk this way.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.920
Well, I have someone to feed!

00:19:38.234 --> 00:19:41.400
Can I say...
- Tell us your point of view.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:45.240
My oldest is 16 now. Right?
-OK.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.960
- The next is army age in 4 years.
- Get to the point!

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:51.600
Wait. Let me finish!

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:52.800
Let me finish.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:59.640
If I and all my friends don't go today,
my kids will tomorrow.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.920
So I came today...

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:07.800
So I came today, so that tomorrow,
my kids don't have to.

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:11.640
I thought I was fighting for our country.

00:20:12.284 --> 00:20:13.521
And why are you here?

00:20:13.677 --> 00:20:15.344
- Yes, why?
- I'll tell you.

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.360
Make it beautiful.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:19.800
was a drug addict.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.154
Fuckin ‘eh!
- I went crazy.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:23.880
I was fucking crazy.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:28.320
I just know I'd have been sucked back in
if I hadn't come here.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.400
I have just one question. May I ask?

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:36.840
To Volodya.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:42.360
Why doesn't Volodya...
value the term 'patriotism'?

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.284
Why?
No idea.

00:20:44.349 --> 00:20:46.380
-What the fuck!
-Be quiet!

00:20:46.432 --> 00:20:48.138
Patriotism exists, but...

00:33:43.752 --> 00:33:44.819
I don't know.

00:33:50.974 --> 00:33:52.415
Let's be quick.

00:33:52.901 --> 00:33:54.950
Don't slow down.

00:37:53.075 --> 00:37:54.664
I don't know.

00:46:31.974 --> 00:46:33.224
Yes.

00:50:39.476 --> 00:50:40.604
Bitch!

00:50:44.641 --> 00:50:46.283
Fucking hell.

00:51:53.921 --> 00:51:55.093
Why?

00:54:55.182 --> 00:54:56.365
What do you think?

00:58:35.074 --> 00:58:39.371
There, over by the boxes.

01:02:17.990 --> 01:02:19.630
And that's my bed.

01:08:57.597 --> 01:09:03.657
And a young commander,

01:09:04.249 --> 01:09:08.155
with his head bashed in,
was carried out.

01:41:57.802 --> 01:41:59.320
it's very scary.

01:50:51.684 --> 01:50:53.794
Calm down, do you hear?

02:04:40.448 --> 02:04:41.394
 Why?

00:20:48.384 --> 00:20:50.280
I need to know...

00:20:50.729 --> 00:20:55.800
If I'm caught in a fight,
I always need to know that I'm right.

00:20:55.825 --> 00:20:58.320
If I'm wrong, I don't fight.
That's how it is here.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.120
Yes, that's it here.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:04.440
We got into a fight with Ukraine,
but I don't feel I'm right.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:23.400
There...

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.400
This is how we self-medicate.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:29.640
For victory.

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:50.400
We'll see how it all ends.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:22:00.240
But I think the losses will be huge.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:19.320
Today, the whole battalion
is leaving for the front.

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:26.880
Surprisingly, command has
tolerated me in the rear so far.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:30.120
But I'm going...

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:34.800
so I don't upset the command...

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:37.440
a bit secretly from them.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:57.240
If they don't catch me
before we leave, of course.

00:22:58.920 --> 00:23:00.840
This all has to be filmed.

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:06.360
I'll try as hard as I can to minimize
consequences for the participants.

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:11.880
To try to tell the story and do no harm.

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.200
We'll see how it ends.

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:43.920
Mechanics, drivers, spotters, operators.

00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:46.775
Are you loaded?

00:23:48.133 --> 00:23:49.560
Almost.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:59.280
Where's Cap? Cap, my brother!

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:04.440
So we're leaving right now?

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:07.560
Leave everything and go as we are?

00:24:20.760 --> 00:24:23.640
Guys, wave for the camera, please.

00:24:26.280 --> 00:24:27.360
You beauties!

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:33.360
In today's video, you will see
how Russian military personnel travel.

00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:37.800
The world's second strongest army.
Imagine how it is in the fourth!

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:39.360
Not knowing where to.

00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:43.800
Nothing changes.

00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:46.560
It's the same as 30 years ago.

00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:52.200
Girl, stop! Don't!

00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:56.280
Don't confuse one dance with another.

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:02.400
Anechka, I'm not drinking.

00:25:03.960 --> 00:25:05.400
I need my cat.

00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:05.160
cat.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.800
A cat?

00:25:07.200 --> 00:25:08.880
Yes, where is she?
Here somewhere.

00:25:09.840 --> 00:25:11.760
She's under the table.

00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:15.840
You don't get it.
No cat means no luck.

00:25:17.520 --> 00:25:19.800
Musya, let's go.

00:25:19.800 --> 00:25:21.960
You've been here long enough.

00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:27.000
Musya, sit.

00:25:30.960 --> 00:25:33.000
Musya, sit quietly.

00:25:51.120 --> 00:25:54.240
Watch it, you have to sit on all that stuff.

00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:17.160
Are they waiting for us?

00:26:17.280 --> 00:26:18.600
In theory, yes.

00:26:20.160 --> 00:26:22.800
I don't know how they drive.

00:26:27.120 --> 00:26:29.760
We're advancing in all directions:

00:26:29.880 --> 00:26:32.640
tanks, infantry, artillery fire.

00:26:32.760 --> 00:26:35.520
We're killed but we survive.

00:26:35.640 --> 00:26:39.000
And again,
we throw ourselves into attack.

00:26:41.880 --> 00:26:45.480
Lena, I'm busy, I can't talk.

00:26:51.720 --> 00:26:57.000
Cheers to life, war be damned...

00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:06.120
We've stopped on the way to the front.

00:27:06.720 --> 00:27:09.120
We sleep in a Soviet nuclear bunker.

00:27:11.640 --> 00:27:13.560
We can't stay here long.

00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:16.440
We've no choice. That's it for now.

00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:21.600
- Everything created by
the people must be protected -

00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:28.200
The move takes two days.

00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:34.440
Everything here feels like a Soviet time capsule.

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:41.760
- Civil Defence's role: defend the people
against weapons of mass destruction -

00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:46.200
The people who created the USSR,

00:27:46.680 --> 00:27:51.240
must be turning in their graves now,
because it's all been destroyed.

00:27:52.320 --> 00:27:54.240
It even came to war.

00:27:58.920 --> 00:28:02.640
After the collapse of the Soviet Union
a confrontation began

00:28:02.760 --> 00:28:05.640
between Eastern and Western Ukraine.

00:28:10.320 --> 00:28:16.560
All the heritage that united us was
being destroyed by Western nationalists:

00:28:17.640 --> 00:28:21.120
demolishing statues of Soviet heroes,

00:28:21.720 --> 00:28:25.440
rewriting textbooks, renaming of streets.

00:28:27.120 --> 00:28:32.280
If we speak Russian, we're like
second class Ukrainians to them.

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:38.160
But for me, the ties between
Russia and Eastern Ukraine

00:28:38.520 --> 00:28:43.800
transcend all borders that
appeared after the collapse of the USSR.

00:28:45.840 --> 00:28:49.800
We are for peace!

00:28:49.825 --> 00:28:52.320
Glory to Labour! -

00:28:52.440 --> 00:28:53.640
- Glory to Labour! -

00:28:53.760 --> 00:28:58.200
Long Live Soviet Trade Unions:
the School of Communism!-

00:28:58.320 --> 00:29:02.568
- Discipline and organisation
are the law for everyone! -

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:12.240
I just remember how
we lived together before.

00:29:14.280 --> 00:29:17.280
Russia and Ukraine
were always inseparable.

00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:25.800
That brotherly Union, I miss it.

00:30:30.120 --> 00:30:32.760
I see these destroyed houses.

00:30:33.120 --> 00:30:38.160
And those poor people
with no electricity, gas, or water.

00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:41.520
It's awful.

00:30:45.720 --> 00:30:47.520
I know what it's like.

00:30:48.360 --> 00:30:51.000
The "dill" [slur for Ukrainians] bombed my house.

00:30:56.760 --> 00:30:59.160
I'd go in, look at the rubble,

00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:03.120
and I just didn't have
the will to do anything.

00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:06.720
I'd sit for an hour thinking...

00:31:09.120 --> 00:31:12.240
About how it could
have been avoided 10 times.

00:31:14.400 --> 00:31:18.000
And about how we're at war
with ourselves.

00:31:20.400 --> 00:31:21.960
Slavs against Slavs.

00:31:23.640 --> 00:31:27.240
It turns out that some Slavs
are for the West,

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:29.880
and some Slavs are for Russia.

00:31:35.520 --> 00:31:38.160
We reached our new base.

00:31:38.400 --> 00:31:41.160
It's a small town 7km from the front.

00:31:42.240 --> 00:31:43.800
The first one went.

00:31:44.640 --> 00:31:45.840
The second went!

00:31:46.440 --> 00:31:47.760
Where's it going?

00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:50.640
There, against the wall.

00:31:51.960 --> 00:31:54.840
Wait, they want to park
the Urals [trucks] there.

00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:06.240
Why are you standing around? Help us!

00:32:20.640 --> 00:32:22.680
Put something under the wheel!

00:32:23.280 --> 00:32:24.360
Move, fuck!

00:32:26.160 --> 00:32:30.260
Back the truck up here.
You're on guard, I'm going.

00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:34.560
Come on, Leha, slowly!

00:32:41.640 --> 00:32:44.640
The battalion medics come for fuel.

00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:51.000
They explain that Code 300 means
'wounded' and Code 200 - 'dead.'

00:32:52.920 --> 00:32:55.200
We'll hear these terms often.

00:33:09.960 --> 00:33:14.400
The evacuation point is where
soldiers are dropped off to find their trenches,

00:33:14.760 --> 00:33:18.600
and where the dead and wounded
are left to be retrieved by the medics.

00:33:19.320 --> 00:33:21.720
- Anyone here?
- Hello.

00:33:34.800 --> 00:33:35.880
Coming with us?
Will you go with us?

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:37.440
- I am going there.
- There?

00:33:38.280 --> 00:33:40.320
OK, let's go. I must find a dude.

00:33:40.368 --> 00:33:43.608
You didn't see a body there?
Fucking close.

00:33:57.597 --> 00:33:59.941
This way? OK, I'll go this way then.

00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:02.520
And you go that way.

00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:04.800
He must be here somewhere.

00:34:05.054 --> 00:34:07.920
If you see a crater, check if he's in there.

00:34:12.480 --> 00:34:14.640
Where are you, bro? Give me a sign.

00:34:27.840 --> 00:34:28.560
Got him?

00:34:29.880 --> 00:34:30.840
Great.

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:37.250
OK, bro, thanks.

00:34:37.345 --> 00:34:39.600
It's flying everywhere!
- We know!

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:46.680
OK, bro, we've come for you. Be cool.

00:34:50.160 --> 00:34:51.600
So heavy, brother.

00:34:59.280 --> 00:35:00.120
Hell.

00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:02.880
Sit down, fuck.

00:35:04.200 --> 00:35:05.400
Fucking bitches.

00:35:06.120 --> 00:35:06.720
Fuck
all.

00:35:06.840 --> 00:35:07.680
Fuck you all.

00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:24.360
He's the battalion's first death, a 'newbie.'

00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:28.920
No one even had a chance
to get to know him.

00:35:52.200 --> 00:35:54.480
Girls, thank you all, you're heroes.

00:35:56.280 --> 00:35:58.560
Looks like a stomach wound.

00:36:02.160 --> 00:36:03.600
He has nothing on him!

00:36:04.320 --> 00:36:06.480
Just a knife and flashlight.

00:36:06.600 --> 00:36:08.160
Well, Nastia, fuck.

00:36:08.760 --> 00:36:10.920
I tell you, he has no papers.

00:36:11.400 --> 00:36:13.800
They said there are. Look carefully.

00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:16.320
His inner pockets.

00:36:16.800 --> 00:36:21.120
I don't know, maybe he has...
pockets in his sweater?

00:36:21.968 --> 00:36:24.488
Here are the 'Girls Like Stars.' Fuck!

00:36:24.960 --> 00:36:27.000
'Stars like her!'

00:36:29.295 --> 00:36:31.200
- A fucking turn.
-'Like her!'

00:36:38.640 --> 00:36:40.560
Nope! No documents.

00:36:44.760 --> 00:36:47.520
Gerda, heating isn't the best idea now.

00:36:47.880 --> 00:36:51.120
Girls, like stars,
shine in the sky till dawn.

00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:55.680
I could fall in love with one,
once and forever, with ease.

00:36:57.480 --> 00:36:58.800
Is there a tag at least?

00:36:59.880 --> 00:37:01.680
Stars like her.

00:37:03.591 --> 00:37:05.193
Girls like stars.

00:37:05.236 --> 00:37:07.920
Damn! I always smell it from afar, fuck.

00:37:11.160 --> 00:37:12.840
There's a tag.

00:37:23.760 --> 00:37:26.280
Want me to open it?
The face, yes.

00:37:48.840 --> 00:37:50.760
What do the guys die for?

00:38:02.408 --> 00:38:04.448
But to take someone over...

00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:08.400
What the fuck is the point?

00:38:10.920 --> 00:38:14.760
What will it change?
Will the war stop?

00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:17.400
Now that's history, fuck!

00:38:17.433 --> 00:38:20.768
Our ancestors and descendants
will know about this.

00:38:20.862 --> 00:38:23.262
What will they think of this shit?

00:38:25.336 --> 00:38:27.256
I mean... Fuck!

00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:43.560
Ukraine, it's a very beautiful country.

00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:46.920
It's like Russia, I can say.

00:38:50.760 --> 00:38:53.970
grew up in a shabby
square like this at Granny's.

00:38:55.320 --> 00:38:58.680
But this fucking war,
it just ruins everything.

00:39:09.960 --> 00:39:11.802
I love our motherland.

00:39:12.103 --> 00:39:14.429
Russia is my motherland.

00:39:14.560 --> 00:39:18.600
Although for me, motherland
begins and ends with my comrades.

00:39:20.640 --> 00:39:23.520
- People live here -

00:39:31.440 --> 00:39:35.760
I recall, at about 7, telling my parents,
'I want to be in the military.'

00:39:36.796 --> 00:39:40.276
They asked, 'What about a family?'
\ I said, 'Fuck it.'

00:39:41.160 --> 00:39:44.760
Comrades are family for me
and I don't need anything more.

00:39:45.938 --> 00:39:50.705
Russia is the traditions
and values we grew up with! -

00:39:58.551 --> 00:40:02.163
- The world's not crap, people are! -

00:40:02.198 --> 00:40:06.480
Whoever wrote this
is fucking Confucius!

00:40:05.640 --> 00:40:06.040
O8

00:40:06.240 --> 00:40:07.240
DA

00:40:08.640 --> 00:40:09.960
Let's roll.

00:40:18.120 --> 00:40:23.400
I didn't tell anyone that I left, nope.

00:40:26.400 --> 00:40:31.800
But while our boys are here,
I'll go nowhere. How could I leave them?

00:41:02.880 --> 00:41:07.320
Pigs! Throw your garbage in the can! -

00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:11.400
Danger to life [in Ukrainian]

00:41:13.800 --> 00:41:15.000
You got through?

00:41:15.960 --> 00:41:17.760
There's no reception.

00:41:24.600 --> 00:41:25.800
Enough!

00:41:37.283 --> 00:41:40.680
- Those who persevere, win -

00:41:43.560 --> 00:41:47.640
I've never climbed
abandoned buildings like this.

00:41:52.440 --> 00:41:55.920
They probably wanted
to build apartments here.

00:42:01.560 --> 00:42:03.720
Hello? Hi sunshine.

00:42:08.880 --> 00:42:11.280
Did you fix your broken nail?

00:42:11.520 --> 00:42:13.800
That's sad.

00:42:15.840 --> 00:42:17.280
I'm listening.

00:42:17.760 --> 00:42:19.200
I'm listening to you.

00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:22.560
Go on, tell me!

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:25.560
Whatever comes to mind.

00:42:37.920 --> 00:42:41.760
This is my first time
on the roof of a nine-story building.

00:42:43.001 --> 00:42:44.768
How beautiful!

00:42:47.160 --> 00:42:48.840
It's breathtaking.

00:42:54.720 --> 00:42:57.240
Where do they keep firing?

00:42:57.710 --> 00:42:59.390
Just into the void...

00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:08.640
Naturally, we'll all lose someone here.

00:43:10.580 --> 00:43:11.880
Boom!

00:43:13.920 --> 00:43:15.480
That was loud.

00:43:20.400 --> 00:43:24.240
There's zero information.
No one really knows anything.

00:43:58.560 --> 00:44:01.800
- Your first time heading to the front too?
- Yeah.

00:44:20.520 --> 00:44:24.600
Watch for birds [drones].
Some fucking silence.

00:44:22.680 --> 00:44:24.106
Watch for birds [drones).

00:44:22.920 --> 00:44:24.106
Watch for birds (drones].

00:44:23.400 --> 00:44:23.694
Watch for birds [drones])

00:44:24.772 --> 00:44:26.400
Calm before the storm.

00:44:26.880 --> 00:44:29.160
We have to go up to the trenches.

00:44:30.960 --> 00:44:33.120
Yes, we need to climb this mountain.

00:44:34.440 --> 00:44:35.760
Speed up, guys.

00:44:38.640 --> 00:44:41.400
OK, from here. No point going higher.

00:44:45.120 --> 00:44:47.760
Look, be careful with the pin.

00:44:49.320 --> 00:44:50.280
Slowly!

00:44:53.520 --> 00:44:55.680
Why's it so tight?

00:44:57.728 --> 00:45:00.008
OK, ready. I can launch.

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:02.400
OK, guys, we're flying.

00:45:21.600 --> 00:45:24.000
Cap, Cap, this is Cartoon. Come in

00:45:28.094 --> 00:45:30.480
Cap, Cap, this is Cartoon. Come in.

00:45:34.680 --> 00:45:36.480
We'll stop and wait.

00:45:48.720 --> 00:45:52.800
I'm expecting him back from a mission.

00:45:54.120 --> 00:45:56.880
It's his first outing. I've already been.

00:45:58.200 --> 00:46:01.200
Cap, this is Cartoon. Come in.
- Cap here.

00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:04.440
Where are you, bro?

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:08.760
Heading for the school
from the nine-story building.

00:46:09.480 --> 00:46:10.320
Roger.

00:46:16.440 --> 00:46:18.600
Look how clean he is!

00:46:19.920 --> 00:46:21.600
My brother!

00:46:24.840 --> 00:46:26.400
Look here.

00:46:26.425 --> 00:46:28.680
What is it?
I took shrapnel.

00:46:29.639 --> 00:46:31.861
- Peace, bro.
Shrapnel?

00:46:34.800 --> 00:46:37.772
My partner's a dickhead.
- What did he do?

00:46:38.160 --> 00:46:43.440
We loaded up the drone grenades,
took off, and his dropped right away.

00:46:44.520 --> 00:46:46.680
I see them fall and turn away.

00:46:46.920 --> 00:46:50.400
It goes off, and a shrapnel
shard splits both my lips.

00:46:53.280 --> 00:46:56.760
- Was your camera always on?
- I hung it here on my chest.

00:46:57.360 --> 00:46:58.440
OK,here.

00:46:59.760 --> 00:47:01.800
OK, guys, we'll take off.

00:47:10.680 --> 00:47:13.920
- This shrapnel fucked me up.
Sorry.

00:47:15.000 --> 00:47:16.440
- Alive? OK?
- Yes.

00:47:17.760 --> 00:47:20.520
Grab it all and let's get out of here.

00:47:32.528 --> 00:47:34.808
Most importantly, we still have balls.

00:47:39.600 --> 00:47:40.800
Run,run.

00:47:47.280 --> 00:47:52.560
The medics poured me a shot.
I said, 'Fuck off with your vodka!'

00:47:57.240 --> 00:47:59.880
Shit, you're shaking.
- My teeth still hurt.

00:48:00.111 --> 00:48:00.951
Of course.

00:48:01.809 --> 00:48:03.129
Let's go home.

00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:11.760
If it had been a bit higher!
Imagine if it hit my temple.

00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:14.400
Fuck! Code 200 and you're home.

00:48:18.600 --> 00:48:22.200
Remember, in the summer,
before we got here?

00:48:22.680 --> 00:48:24.600
Before we were drafted.

00:48:25.560 --> 00:48:28.800
A wasp stung my lip,
remember the photo?

00:48:29.520 --> 00:48:32.520
Yes! Botox.
A fucking lip like that!

00:48:33.840 --> 00:48:35.400
Botox.

00:48:47.760 --> 00:48:49.440
Tire. Tire. Reply to Amin.

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:52.560
Find out the nature of the wound.

00:48:56.160 --> 00:48:59.400
Amin, this is Tire.
Shrapnel near the heart, over.

00:49:00.720 --> 00:49:02.280
Understood, over.

00:49:22.920 --> 00:49:26.400
Chief, there's a war on!
You're too gentle with the van.

00:49:26.880 --> 00:49:28.200
We'll fix it.

00:49:31.320 --> 00:49:32.760
That's it, stop.

00:49:39.240 --> 00:49:41.400
- Enough!
- That's it.

00:49:43.560 --> 00:49:45.720
Put something under my head!

00:49:46.560 --> 00:49:47.520
Let's go!

00:49:48.360 --> 00:49:50.400
Be patient, brother.

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:54.360
How are you feeling?
- OK. It really hurts, fuck.

00:49:54.720 --> 00:49:57.840
Chief, drive carefully! But fast, damn!

00:50:00.840 --> 00:50:04.314
Be patient, please, just a little longer.

00:50:04.825 --> 00:50:07.440
Your arm's tattooed! You never told me.

00:50:13.199 --> 00:50:14.399
Cannula!

00:50:15.960 --> 00:50:18.480
Master, they took him, he left.

00:50:23.160 --> 00:50:25.320
It's OK, brother, it'll be fine.

00:50:27.120 --> 00:50:30.240
My son isn't in school yet,
I can't die now.

00:50:30.600 --> 00:50:32.400
You're lucky.

00:50:32.640 --> 00:50:36.480
Yeah. A few centimetres lower
and you'd be out of luck.

00:50:40.680 --> 00:50:42.120
Give me a cigarette.

00:50:42.360 --> 00:50:44.160
You're not allowed brother.

00:50:47.280 --> 00:50:49.680
- I want to fucking smoke.
- OK.

00:51:15.600 --> 00:51:20.400
- Don't follow me, I'm lost myself. -

00:51:36.971 --> 00:51:40.691
You've heard that Russian troops
were accused of war crimes?

00:51:41.640 --> 00:51:42.720
A war crime?

00:51:42.840 --> 00:51:46.440
War crimes. That civilians were killed,
people were r****.

00:51:47.400 --> 00:51:50.160
- What do you think, is it true?
- I think it's not true.

00:51:50.989 --> 00:51:53.269
It couldn't happen?
It couldn't happen.

00:52:00.600 --> 00:52:03.000
Well, I've seen lots of people.

00:52:04.200 --> 00:52:05.400
Many.

00:52:05.855 --> 00:52:08.375
Some are capable of a lot.

00:52:08.400 --> 00:52:12.480
But to go up to civilians
who've done nothing to you,

00:52:12.840 --> 00:52:16.800
and kill them, r*** them, bury them?

00:52:16.825 --> 00:52:21.265
No, Russian troops couldn't do that,
they wouldn't. Why would they?

00:52:21.840 --> 00:52:23.880
People just live their lives.

00:52:27.480 --> 00:52:30.240
Why ruin that person's life?

00:52:30.960 --> 00:52:32.880
But we invaded their country?

00:52:40.320 --> 00:52:44.520
We kind of invaded..
Maybe not of our own free will.
565
00:52:44,545 --&gt; 00:52:44,160
We kind of invaded...

00:52:46.560 --> 00:52:48.240
There was an order.

00:52:48.491 --> 00:52:49.811
We went in.

00:52:52.560 --> 00:52:54.960
You think the order was right?

00:53:01.044 --> 00:53:05.651
Cap, do you have a 7.62?
- Check my jacket. Left pocket.

00:53:22.560 --> 00:53:23.760
- What are you doing?
- Adding the bullet...

00:53:23.880 --> 00:53:25.560
What are you doing?

00:53:27.360 --> 00:53:28.680
to my tag.

00:53:31.920 --> 00:53:33.240
Just a memento.

00:53:34.560 --> 00:53:35.880
A memento.

00:53:36.273 --> 00:53:38.956
I'd get it if it had come out of your chest

00:53:41.595 --> 00:53:44.235
- You want a bullet in my chest?
- No.

00:53:44.640 --> 00:53:45.840
 That's that then.

00:53:48.371 --> 00:53:49.451
It's broken.

00:53:51.010 --> 00:53:52.210
Let's test it now.

00:53:54.360 --> 00:53:55.320
Of course...

00:54:00.120 --> 00:54:02.160
Fucking hell!

00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:05.280
That was dangerous, fuck.

00:54:05.400 --> 00:54:09.000
We should all be 200
and sent home by now.

00:54:09.360 --> 00:54:10.200
Done!

00:54:23.400 --> 00:54:26.400
That's all. It drops, pierces the capsule...

00:54:26.629 --> 00:54:29.757
- Where's the tailpiece from?
- The guys rigged it.

00:54:31.030 --> 00:54:33.840
I just need to refine this nail mechanism.
- The guys rigged it.

00:54:35.280 --> 00:54:37.800
Where did I put that little drill bit?

00:54:41.911 --> 00:54:44.400
For the uninitiated, what's it for?

00:54:45.120 --> 00:54:46.680
To kill.

00:54:51.720 --> 00:54:54.043
How right is all this?

00:55:02.171 --> 00:55:03.251
What do I think?

00:55:03.960 --> 00:55:06.240
What should I think? Tell me.

00:55:06.589 --> 00:55:09.709
- What exactly?

00:55:10.320 --> 00:55:13.920
All of it, making drone grenades to...
- I'd say...

00:55:15.240 --> 00:55:18.120
it's either me or them.

00:55:18.876 --> 00:55:23.520
Well, I'm doing this for myself,

00:55:24.480 --> 00:55:26.400
to survive.

00:55:33.720 --> 00:55:38.400
You ask such questions,
I don't even know how to answer them.

00:55:41.280 --> 00:55:45.240
Have you thought about it?
- What should I think about?

00:55:45.840 --> 00:55:50.400
That we're on their land and we
should turn around and fuck off?

00:55:50.400 --> 00:55:52.920
Leave our guys on their own?

00:55:53.280 --> 00:55:57.840
Is that what we should have done?
Being on their land. Invading.

00:55:58.200 --> 00:56:01.560
And them bombing their own people
for eight years is nothing?

00:56:03.360 --> 00:56:05.280
How many children died?

00:56:05.880 --> 00:56:07.680
And old men and women.

00:56:08.400 --> 00:56:10.200
They bombed their own people.

00:56:18.120 --> 00:56:21.240
We're a bit wrong, they're a bit wrong.

00:56:21.480 --> 00:56:24.480
For sure, that's what it is.

00:56:30.240 --> 00:56:32.400
I'm just doing my job right now.

00:56:33.120 --> 00:56:34.320
Oh shit.

00:56:37.680 --> 00:56:39.960
Shit, I broke the drill bit.

00:56:42.600 --> 00:56:44.880
Damn! I glued my fingers together.

00:56:45.120 --> 00:56:49.560
- From Cartoon to Cap,
together to the end, brother -

00:57:09.240 --> 00:57:10.920
Mario! Come on, fuck.

00:57:20.640 --> 00:57:22.440
Fucking volunteers.

00:57:22.800 --> 00:57:24.000
Tourists.

00:57:25.320 --> 00:57:27.480
We're not in the military now.

00:57:33.600 --> 00:57:35.520
You go there often?

00:57:38.520 --> 00:57:44.640
Humanitarian aid from the 'great'
United Russia Party doesn't get there.

00:57:46.560 --> 00:57:48.600
So the medics take it.

00:57:50.880 --> 00:57:53.400
It's a beautiful village.

00:57:54.720 --> 00:57:56.400
26 people.

00:57:56.760 --> 00:57:58.800
They're bombing there now?

00:57:58.920 --> 00:58:03.000
Yes. The Commander asked why the fuck
are we, idiots, going there.

00:58:08.280 --> 00:58:11.400
Somewhere round here, by a blue gate.

00:58:14.280 --> 00:58:18.360
This whole war is like
stagnant gonorrhoea.

00:58:19.320 --> 00:58:21.480
It's neither here nor there.

00:58:32.280 --> 00:58:33.847
Where to?

00:58:39.985 --> 00:58:42.600
I'll sit down and organise it.

00:58:43.434 --> 00:58:45.840
Fellow villagers are so happy!

00:58:46.440 --> 00:58:50.041
I go out at 8 am
and the boxes are waiting.

00:58:51.600 --> 00:58:54.840
'Where's this from?'
I say, soldiers brought it.

00:58:55.560 --> 00:58:58.320
Amin, report to Yamal's location.

00:58:58.680 --> 00:59:02.160
We need to remove shrapnel
from a leg, over.

00:59:03.600 --> 00:59:06.120
Your truck's no good.

00:59:07.440 --> 00:59:11.160
That '300', are they alive or wounded?

00:59:11.640 --> 00:59:15.480
They're the wounded.
Then it's not so bad.

00:59:15.887 --> 00:59:19.800
I'm so afraid that
the dead are carried around.

00:59:21.720 --> 00:59:24.120
Amin, received, understood.

00:59:24.360 --> 00:59:25.920
Roger, Amin.

00:59:26.280 --> 00:59:29.280
- Are you often bombed here?
Yesterday, no.
643
00:59:29,305 --&gt; 00:59:29,280
- Yesterday, no.

00:59:29.760 --> 00:59:33.240
The day before yesterday,
it hit behind the raspberries.

00:59:33.720 --> 00:59:36.480
And three days ago, behind the kitchen.

00:59:37.560 --> 00:59:39.240
Come and have a look.

00:59:39.840 --> 00:59:42.000
Come and see. I'll show you.

00:59:46.440 --> 00:59:50.280
- Thank you so much. God bless you!
- You're welcome.
649
00:59:50,305 --&gt; 00:59:50,280
You're welcome.

00:59:50.760 --> 00:59:52.920
It's good to have it all in boxes.

00:59:54.000 --> 01:00:00.120
We'll figure it out, I'll get Nina and Nadia.
We'll divide it all up for 26 people.

01:00:01.978 --> 01:00:05.385
Thank you very much.
Come on, I'll show you.

01:00:10.320 --> 01:00:12.000
There's a big pit there.

01:00:13.800 --> 01:00:14.760
See the craters there?

01:00:18.120 --> 01:00:20.640
- Why don't you leave?
- Where to?

01:00:22.320 --> 01:00:27.000
They've already gone,
those who had transport and money.

01:00:29.520 --> 01:00:30.600
It's my...

01:00:31.320 --> 01:00:36.840
dream not to die, not to be killed.
I ask God, 'God, help us survive.

01:00:37.320 --> 01:00:40.800
Help end this war, so they stop shooting.'

01:00:40.920 --> 01:00:46.800
And this killing! Ukraine and Russia,
you're brothers. Why kill each other?

01:00:50.160 --> 01:00:51.840
That's how things are.

01:00:53.640 --> 01:00:55.680
Of course, we're all for Russia.

01:00:55.822 --> 01:00:58.462
Well, a guy on Lenin St., Vitka,

01:00:58.900 --> 01:01:03.720
he had a store and always spoke out,
but he's gone somewhere.

01:01:04.200 --> 01:01:06.000
And why are people for Russia?

01:01:06.240 --> 01:01:09.360
I don't know. You see, I went to school...

01:01:10.320 --> 01:01:14.280
We had a portrait of Lenin
hanging over the blackboard.

01:01:14.542 --> 01:01:18.022
It said: 'study, study, study,
as Great Lenin willed.'

01:01:18.360 --> 01:01:19.800
Ukraine is against Lenin!

01:01:20.388 --> 01:01:22.123
We studied everything Russian.

01:01:22.159 --> 01:01:27.022
Our class represented Kazakhstan,
one of our 15 Republics.

01:01:27.480 --> 01:01:33.360
Each class put on concerts
and wore their national dress.

01:01:33.731 --> 01:01:36.731
We should be friends in peace,
we should be friends.

01:01:36.840 --> 01:01:38.880
I was used to it, I studied it...

01:01:39.960 --> 01:01:42.480
I believed in it all!

01:01:54.120 --> 01:01:58.320
I usually walk with two sticks,
but now I have one.

01:02:04.440 --> 01:02:08.400
My knees are gone.
I worked in the mine for 28 years.

01:02:09.840 --> 01:02:11.400
I'll find a flashlight.

01:02:13.189 --> 01:02:17.934
My son sleeps here on this cot
made of bricks and planks.

01:02:20.280 --> 01:02:21.600
You've been here a year?

01:02:22.680 --> 01:02:25.800
Since March, the end of March.
Yes, a year.

01:02:28.560 --> 01:02:30.120
I blame...

01:02:30.491 --> 01:02:33.971
It was America that got involved, I think.

01:02:35.782 --> 01:02:38.902
Well, Ukraine joining NATO or whatever.

01:02:42.720 --> 01:02:45.480
God forbid Ukraine breaks through here.

01:02:45.720 --> 01:02:49.440
That scares me a lot.
I think Ukraine will kill us all.

01:02:49.560 --> 01:02:51.840
For talking to Russia, and so on.

01:02:53.520 --> 01:02:56.280
I think we'll never make peace
with Ukraine.

01:02:57.720 --> 01:02:59.280
Never.

01:03:01.920 --> 01:03:03.480
Mikhailovna!

01:03:44.280 --> 01:03:47.760
Let's go back, in case we have
to hide in the basement.

01:04:16.800 --> 01:04:19.200
This stove probably hadn't
been cleaned for a year.

01:04:28.320 --> 01:04:30.480
I miss home.

01:04:33.960 --> 01:04:35.640
I miss my buddies.

01:04:40.800 --> 01:04:43.126
My garden was awesome...

01:04:43.349 --> 01:04:46.200
and the vineyards were kick-ass!

01:04:52.440 --> 01:04:54.360
The weekends...

01:04:55.341 --> 01:04:57.861
a day would start with a trip...

01:05:04.440 --> 01:05:08.280
to amusement parks with the children.

01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:16.680
And ended...

01:05:17.520 --> 01:05:20.280
with a barbecue in the yard with friends.

01:05:31.800 --> 01:05:35.400
Yeah, those were really good times.

01:05:42.240 --> 01:05:48.600
In 2014, when Ukrainian forces
began bombing Donetsk, it was brutal.

01:05:53.640 --> 01:05:57.120
I drove out with my children
under shelling.

01:05:55.320 --> 01:05:55.560
I drove out with
children

01:05:59.760 --> 01:06:02.411
Of course, Donetsk rosee up.

01:06:02.880 --> 01:06:05.880
Most men joined the [separatist] militia.

01:06:07.690 --> 01:06:10.450
I spent roughly 3 months in the militia.

01:06:12.949 --> 01:06:15.349
Now, there's no life in Donetsk.

01:06:17.160 --> 01:06:19.200
Now everyone's scattered.

01:06:20.280 --> 01:06:21.720
Some killed...

01:06:22.800 --> 01:06:23.640
some somewhere.

01:06:40.297 --> 01:06:43.126
...of NATO caliber, 155 mm.

01:06:43.202 --> 01:06:48.360
Yasinovataya (Donetsk region) and
Panteleimonovka village were also hit.

01:06:50.001 --> 01:06:52.713
I came here to help people.
To protect them.

01:06:54.600 --> 01:06:59.280
Maybe this nightmare they've been
living in since 2014 would end.

01:07:01.865 --> 01:07:05.640
But the reality wasn't
at all what I expected.

01:07:14.045 --> 01:07:16.440
Where did you find
a patriotic newspaper?

01:07:18.480 --> 01:07:19.680
They bring them.

01:07:19.800 --> 01:07:21.000
Red Star-

01:07:21.120 --> 01:07:22.800
Basically, propaganda.

01:07:23.640 --> 01:07:26.760
- Our Spiritual Weapon:
Our Ancestors' Military Tradition -

01:07:27.000 --> 01:07:31.800
In fact, what's written
and shown on TV isn't real.

01:07:34.920 --> 01:07:39.000
It's dangerous because
after watching TV, I volunteered...

01:07:39.960 --> 01:07:44.520
let's say, as a patriot, for this SMO
[Special Military Operation].

01:07:47.520 --> 01:07:49.200
I volunteered for six months.

01:07:49.440 --> 01:07:53.400
Now I'm already
in my seventh month here.

01:07:55.538 --> 01:07:59.258
They said the only way
back to Russia is 'feet first' [dead).

01:08:02.181 --> 01:08:02.975
If I'd known that, I wouldn't have come.

01:08:03.007 --> 01:08:03.644
If l'd known that, I wouldn't have come.

01:08:05.400 --> 01:08:07.680
Because I too had life plans.

01:08:12.000 --> 01:08:14.400
There's no forward movement.

01:08:14.425 --> 01:08:17.760
I think the conflict is artificially prolonged.

01:08:18.000 --> 01:08:20.160
Because it benefits someone.

01:08:21.960 --> 01:08:23.520
We don't want war.

01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:26.280
We don't want to kill, or to die.

01:08:27.720 --> 01:08:29.640
What do you think you'll do?

01:08:30.120 --> 01:08:31.440
Keep on serving.

01:08:33.600 --> 01:08:36.720
Neither they [Ukrainians) nor we have a choice.

01:08:39.600 --> 01:08:42.840
The tanks rumbled on the field.

01:08:42.960 --> 01:08:46.800
Soldiers went into their last battle.

01:08:46.835 --> 01:08:53.121
And a young commander,

01:08:53.146 --> 01:08:57.106
with his head bashed in,
was carried out.

01:09:32.760 --> 01:09:34.200
Happy Birthday, bro!

01:10:08.065 --> 01:10:12.480
Pour champagne on it,
like when you buy a family car!

01:10:19.800 --> 01:10:23.520
I kind of spilled an energy drink in here.

01:10:24.360 --> 01:10:28.560
So much shit! You're scared
to press anything and fuck it up.

01:10:29.280 --> 01:10:35.400
Look, press the rangefinder with
your index finger. Here's the 'SCT.'

01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:41.160
They didn't even explain what it is.
They just said, 'You'll need it', that's it.

01:10:42.720 --> 01:10:45.120
Fuck, it's a USSR label.

01:10:46.200 --> 01:10:48.720
Even though it's 2023 in Russia.

01:10:50.280 --> 01:10:51.960
Cartoon, fire!

01:10:56.760 --> 01:10:59.400
Come on, start up your baby!

01:11:36.480 --> 01:11:39.240
When we arrived, at first there was fear.

01:11:40.800 --> 01:11:43.800
And then somehow it didn't matter.

01:11:47.041 --> 01:11:51.960
What you want or don't want isn't a thing.
Here, have to' means 'have to'.

01:11:47.520 --> 01:11:49.586
Here, 'have to means 'have to'.

01:11:56.160 --> 01:11:59.160
I don't see the concept of
fair or unfair here.

01:12:01.800 --> 01:12:05.520
They and we shell each other
almost the same.

01:12:11.160 --> 01:12:14.280
- When did the shooting start?
- At 10:30.

01:12:18.936 --> 01:12:21.481
-Whoa!
Incoming, incoming.

01:12:22.560 --> 01:12:25.560
I told you, fuck. Get down...

01:12:26.280 --> 01:12:29.193
Nastia, come in, please.
- Coming, coming.

01:12:29.282 --> 01:12:31.920
Something's on fire.
No, nothing's burning.

01:12:41.640 --> 01:12:43.800
Now they'll adjust and hit again.

01:12:44.640 --> 01:12:46.920
Now they'll reload
and start again.

01:12:48.360 --> 01:12:51.960
Oh, fuck.
- It's a cannon if it takes time to reload.
768
01:50:06,985 --&gt; 01:12:51,960
- Oh, fuck.
769
01:12:51,985 --&gt; 01:12:51,960
It's a cannon if it takes time to reload.

01:12:52.061 --> 01:12:53.389
They're adjusting.

01:12:54.360 --> 01:12:56.160
It's coming!

01:12:59.160 --> 01:13:00.360
2 minutes!

01:13:00.480 --> 01:13:02.640
They're clearly hitting the house.

01:13:04.800 --> 01:13:06.240
That was three.

01:13:06.720 --> 01:13:08.160
The doors must be shut.

01:13:08.280 --> 01:13:10.415
- No!
- Bricks will fly in.
777
01:13:12,025 --&gt; 01:13:09,960
No!
Bricks will fly in.

01:13:10.440 --> 01:13:12.000
Or let's get the fuck out.

01:13:12.120 --> 01:13:15.840
- We can't go anywhere now.
- There's a bird [drone] up there.
780
01:13:15,865 --&gt; 01:13:15,240
There's a bird [drone] up there.

01:13:16.777 --> 01:13:18.457
Ours are fucking quiet.

01:13:19.800 --> 01:13:21.360
They'll start late, as usual.

01:13:23.520 --> 01:13:25.560
It's not like this in the trenches.

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:29.280
It's easier to handle there.

01:13:32.880 --> 01:13:34.560
Shit. We lived a good life.

01:13:34.920 --> 01:13:36.480
We all move out today.

01:13:38.077 --> 01:13:40.200
Fuck, didn't you smoke
enough outside?

01:13:40.680 --> 01:13:42.120
We're suffocating in here.

01:13:46.440 --> 01:13:48.960
Ready. Ready. Ready...

01:13:51.360 --> 01:13:52.560
It's not for us.

01:13:52.680 --> 01:13:54.120
No, that was closer.

01:13:54.600 --> 01:13:57.000
- It's a long way off.
- Probably a tank.

01:13:57.840 --> 01:13:59.400
A mass grave.

01:13:59.520 --> 01:14:02.160
- Where are you going? Stay.
- Give me a smoke.

01:14:02.520 --> 01:14:04.320
Hey, what are you, an addict?

01:14:08.760 --> 01:14:10.320
Now it's closer again.

01:14:13.200 --> 01:14:15.480
Where are you going? Smoke in here.

01:14:18.000 --> 01:14:18.840
Ready!

01:14:25.800 --> 01:14:27.840
It's a tank! I tell you, damn it.

01:14:30.120 --> 01:14:32.400
A cannon can't fire that fast.

01:14:33.720 --> 01:14:35.760
Listen. Maybe it's ours?

01:14:36.600 --> 01:14:38.160
Ours are totally silent.

01:14:38.760 --> 01:14:41.760
These are ours.
- Ours, ours...

01:14:42.600 --> 01:14:45.000
How fucking long did it take them?

01:14:58.800 --> 01:15:00.960
20 minutes passed.

01:15:03.240 --> 01:15:05.640
Quiet, quiet. It's a birdie [drone]!

01:15:06.000 --> 01:15:06.960
Quiet!

01:15:11.520 --> 01:15:13.200
A bee!

01:15:16.680 --> 01:15:18.960
Still, it was buzzing.

01:15:25.571 --> 01:15:29.175
- It's a hornet.
- Yes, they sound the same.

01:15:31.210 --> 01:15:32.410
Let's see now.

01:15:32.531 --> 01:15:33.731
OK, I'm off.

01:15:34.908 --> 01:15:38.069
- It's OK.
- At intervals, two at a time.

01:15:38.425 --> 01:15:41.280
Good, let's go now.
Sure, let's go.

01:15:47.280 --> 01:15:51.960
I wake up each morning and think
of the guys lying in the ground.

01:15:52.440 --> 01:15:54.360
They won't see the sun,

01:15:55.680 --> 01:15:59.880
or the sky, won't see or talk
to their parents.

01:16:01.811 --> 01:16:03.011
Starting a war is very easy.

01:16:03.960 --> 01:16:06.960
But to finish it, try doing that.

01:16:07.440 --> 01:16:09.000
Was it scary?

01:16:27.562 --> 01:16:30.878
Are we fucking off?
- Yes, yes. Let's fuck off!

01:16:39.120 --> 01:16:39.840
Anastasia, get in.

01:16:41.400 --> 01:16:43.320
- Altitude, 57.
- Altitude, 57.

01:16:44.977 --> 01:16:48.347
- So guys, ready to party?
- We're ready.

01:16:48.960 --> 01:16:50.880
Time to prepare?

01:16:51.480 --> 01:16:52.800
7 minutes.

01:16:55.920 --> 01:16:58.200
Aim and report when ready.
- Copy.

01:16:58.548 --> 01:17:02.388
46... 640.

01:17:03.360 --> 01:17:06.120
An anti-tank launcher is firing at us.

01:17:07.680 --> 01:17:11.640
Confirm, 46... 640... 46... 640...

01:17:26.160 --> 01:17:27.840
It didn't kill you?
Nope.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:32.880
What command?!
There was no command!

01:17:34.680 --> 01:17:36.000
Fuck! You're crazy.

01:17:37.800 --> 01:17:38.640
It could've killed us!

01:17:47.410 --> 01:17:48.370
Fire, fire!

01:18:03.960 --> 01:18:04.800
107

01:18:08.520 --> 01:18:10.800
Spikey, Mario and Chemist.

01:18:10.920 --> 01:18:12.480
Are these all yours? Over.

01:18:13.200 --> 01:18:15.360
Yes, all mine, all mine.

01:18:16.963 --> 01:18:19.697
200, for sure?
Three 200s?

01:18:20.760 --> 01:18:23.400
No one can get to them yet, over.

01:18:24.000 --> 01:18:25.560
Tire, Amin receiving.

01:18:26.520 --> 01:18:28.560
Say again, three 200s?

01:18:30.240 --> 01:18:32.880
Three 200s from the medical unit.

01:18:34.680 --> 01:18:37.800
No one can get to them yet. Over.

01:18:38.966 --> 01:18:40.406
Fuck this shit!

01:19:01.560 --> 01:19:02.880
Left here.

01:19:05.520 --> 01:19:07.680
Pull over at the barrier.

01:19:11.880 --> 01:19:14.280
There's a fucking war going on here.

01:19:16.800 --> 01:19:18.360
Swat! Let me in!

01:19:18.720 --> 01:19:21.840
- Look, he's actually aiming his gun.
- Yeah, right.

01:19:24.000 --> 01:19:26.760
That's my unit for fuck's sake, Swat!

01:19:28.560 --> 01:19:30.120
Please.

01:19:30.960 --> 01:19:33.840
Please, let me in alone, at least.

01:19:39.120 --> 01:19:41.160
Don't fucking shoot, fuck.

01:19:41.400 --> 01:19:43.560
Fucking military.

01:19:44.160 --> 01:19:46.800
What a clusterfuck.

01:19:51.120 --> 01:19:54.360
Get the fuck back in there!

01:19:54.720 --> 01:19:56.400
This is how it fucking is.

01:19:57.120 --> 01:19:59.160
What a joke.

01:19:59.520 --> 01:20:00.840
Circus, huh?

01:20:10.320 --> 01:20:12.000
You're like kids, fuck.

01:20:12.960 --> 01:20:14.280
May 1?

01:20:17.520 --> 01:20:19.200
A great time to argue.

01:20:21.840 --> 01:20:23.160
Go right!

01:20:31.800 --> 01:20:33.480
Mario's fucked up.

01:21:04.800 --> 01:21:05.640
Fucking morons.

01:21:18.360 --> 01:21:19.800
A little closer to you.

01:21:26.520 --> 01:21:29.400
Amin, let's go.
It turns out one was left.

01:21:29.520 --> 01:21:30.840
Anton was left behind.

01:21:31.560 --> 01:21:33.960
They said one didn't die right away.

01:21:34.680 --> 01:21:37.920
Spikey died instantly,
did you see his neck?

01:21:38.400 --> 01:21:40.200
Wind, Amin, let's go!

01:21:40.560 --> 01:21:42.840
Guys, go. They'll see us and fire.

01:21:44.400 --> 01:21:45.480
Let's go.

01:22:08.520 --> 01:22:10.320
Fucking Polish mortar.

01:22:10.440 --> 01:22:12.480
You don't hear it coming.

01:22:15.000 --> 01:22:18.360
It killed three with one hit.

01:22:51.960 --> 01:22:54.360
I'm most sorry for Chemist.

01:22:57.120 --> 01:22:59.160
He said he was scared.

01:23:07.320 --> 01:23:09.840
It was his first day. His first time.

01:23:10.200 --> 01:23:11.400
The first!

01:23:22.699 --> 01:23:25.699
One day he came to me and said:

01:23:25.825 --> 01:23:27.628
"Damn...

01:23:28.800 --> 01:23:31.680
Life was just starting to get good,
it was all fine.

01:23:32.760 --> 01:23:37.440
Life with my wife was amazing,
work was great, just like a fairy tale.

01:23:38.160 --> 01:23:41.160
Then war comes along and I'm drafted.'

01:23:42.000 --> 01:23:43.443
Fuck.

01:23:58.560 --> 01:23:59.640
Hello?

01:24:00.480 --> 01:24:03.240
I'm calling about your husband.

01:24:04.800 --> 01:24:06.360
He died on Sunday.

01:24:09.120 --> 01:24:11.400
My condolences to you.

01:24:15.000 --> 01:24:18.840
I'm in command of a medical unit,
he was in my unit.

01:24:19.200 --> 01:24:23.280
I don't know when they'll call officially,
so I'm calling you myself.

01:24:26.160 --> 01:24:30.240
A shell flew in.
Three people died at once.

01:24:33.360 --> 01:24:35.400
He died on the spot.

01:24:40.800 --> 01:24:42.360
Be strong.

01:24:44.400 --> 01:24:45.840
My condolences.

01:24:48.960 --> 01:24:50.640
I'm sorry.

01:25:12.840 --> 01:25:13.920
Is it far?

01:25:14.640 --> 01:25:16.440
Another 2 kilometres.

01:25:18.840 --> 01:25:21.000
Give me a cigarette too.

01:25:27.600 --> 01:25:29.640
God willing, it will all be fine.

01:25:31.604 --> 01:25:33.644
They said that yesterday too.

01:25:39.360 --> 01:25:41.400
Three 200s.

01:25:44.880 --> 01:25:45.000
DI

01:25:52.800 --> 01:25:54.360
I'm not here.

01:25:58.440 --> 01:26:01.200
My personnel file is lost.

01:26:03.600 --> 01:26:05.520
No salary...

01:26:05.640 --> 01:26:08.400
I'm not on the unit list.

01:26:11.400 --> 01:26:13.920
They said, 'Keep serving' and 'good-bye.'

01:26:16.680 --> 01:26:20.400
Strawberries will be here soon.

01:26:23.400 --> 01:26:25.200
The bags are fucking white.

01:26:30.720 --> 01:26:32.400
Keep your distance.

01:26:33.960 --> 01:26:36.840
So that if anyone gets hit,
the others won't.

01:27:10.800 --> 01:27:11.640
They're close.

01:27:12.720 --> 01:27:14.160
500 metres.

01:27:19.320 --> 01:27:20.400
They shout...

01:27:21.752 --> 01:27:24.455
'Russians, surrender!'
'Occupiers.'

01:27:24.480 --> 01:27:27.240
'Occupiers!' Fuck you in the ass!

01:27:29.640 --> 01:27:34.200
The Russian anthem is played
at full blast on the loudspeaker at 5 am.

01:27:36.000 --> 01:27:40.800
What do they play for us?
They play the Ukrainian anthem.

01:27:42.840 --> 01:27:44.880
Well, let's just mark it out.

01:27:46.800 --> 01:27:49.320
We should dig the trenches faster.

01:27:57.945 --> 01:28:00.277
Is that a bird (drone] flying?

01:28:03.120 --> 01:28:04.920
No, it's the river.

01:28:15.600 --> 01:28:18.000
For the last two months,

01:28:18.240 --> 01:28:21.000
I got nothing for being on the front line.

01:28:23.160 --> 01:28:26.760
I didn't get my additional pay
after I was wounded either.

01:28:39.120 --> 01:28:42.240
So when your contract ends,
you'll get drafted?

01:28:42.600 --> 01:28:46.501
Mine ended two months ago already.
Everyone's has.
932
01:28:46,800 --&gt; 01:28:46,320
- Mine ended two months ago already.

01:28:55.320 --> 01:28:58.755
Idon't...
How much did you get this month?

01:28:58.800 --> 01:29:00.120
I got nothing.

01:29:02.400 --> 01:29:06.720
My family... they were threatened
with eviction if they didn't pay.

01:29:08.280 --> 01:29:12.480
Yesterday, I borrowed some money
from the drafted boys.

01:29:22.811 --> 01:29:27.371
If I'd known this would happen,
I'd be damned if l'd have signed up.

01:29:43.353 --> 01:29:45.273
What a situation...

01:29:54.960 --> 01:29:57.000
I don't give a damn.

01:29:59.880 --> 01:30:01.200
I need money.

01:30:06.720 --> 01:30:08.760
It's the only way.

01:30:36.600 --> 01:30:40.200
I can't say anything now.
I can't think until I'm home.

01:30:49.800 --> 01:30:53.520
But I think, 100%, it'll drag me back.

01:30:57.000 --> 01:31:00.000
It's a strange pull.

01:31:00.120 --> 01:31:04.440
I can't describe it, but it's there.

01:31:05.640 --> 01:31:07.680
It's a kind of habit.

01:31:11.520 --> 01:31:12.240
Thanks.

01:31:14.280 --> 01:31:16.440
Can you imagine? I forgot what floor.

01:31:17.873 --> 01:31:21.120
You forgot your floor?
forgot which floor.

01:31:23.880 --> 01:31:26.400
I think the 12th.

01:31:32.520 --> 01:31:33.720
Please come in.

01:31:40.560 --> 01:31:45.240
For abandoning the front,
llya risks criminal prosecution.

01:31:48.960 --> 01:31:52.200
But because he's 50,
he might get written off.

01:31:54.480 --> 01:31:55.800
Hi.

01:32:01.719 --> 01:32:05.094
Daddy!
My pretty little thing.

01:32:10.320 --> 01:32:12.120
Hi, sleepyhead.

01:32:14.760 --> 01:32:18.960
Meanwhile, the battalion
is moved to a tougher front.

01:32:34.078 --> 01:32:36.656
We've been hit. Film this!

01:32:36.840 --> 01:32:39.120
- Film it!
- What happened?

01:32:39.960 --> 01:32:41.880
We got our asses kicked a bit.

01:32:42.840 --> 01:32:45.480
I'm fucked if I'll ride
by that window again!

01:32:45.720 --> 01:32:47.880
Can you believe it?

01:32:48.120 --> 01:32:49.560
How lucky you are!

01:32:51.360 --> 01:32:52.920
The glass is gone!

01:32:53.280 --> 01:32:55.200
'Fuckin' eh!', I thought.

01:32:56.640 --> 01:32:59.160
They moved the whole
brigade overnight to Bakhmut.

01:33:03.360 --> 01:33:06.840
It's the toughest front.
The Bakhmut front.

01:33:08.400 --> 01:33:10.800
It almost killed me, and I'm happy.

01:33:12.120 --> 01:33:14.400
This tire got slashed.

01:33:18.480 --> 01:33:21.960
It's so confusing here,
I don't even know what we're fighting for.

01:33:25.920 --> 01:33:27.360
Not even a clue.

01:33:30.600 --> 01:33:33.360
I've seen so much here
over these 10 months.

01:33:35.640 --> 01:33:37.680
Now, I just want to go home.

01:33:39.240 --> 01:33:43.320
Where no one shoots or kills anyone.

01:33:45.480 --> 01:33:47.400
Quiet, peace.

01:33:49.920 --> 01:33:51.480
But there's no option.

01:33:55.440 --> 01:33:58.200
I'm willing to give my life formy country.

01:33:58.440 --> 01:34:00.240
I'm a Russian patriot.

01:34:03.000 --> 01:34:04.560
Yes, I'm a patriot.

01:34:09.840 --> 01:34:12.600
A lot has changed here...

01:34:13.680 --> 01:34:17.760
Many have died, many wounded,
and a change of command.

01:34:19.779 --> 01:34:24.167
The new commander, I am told, is against my presence.

01:34:26.760 --> 01:34:28.800
But he doesn't live here with the troops,

01:34:29.400 --> 01:34:33.480
so I should be able to avoid him
and film a bit longer.

01:34:46.200 --> 01:34:48.480
He is carved out of flint and steel.

01:34:48.840 --> 01:34:50.160
Brilliant.

01:34:50.880 --> 01:34:54.240
I watched it and just cried.

01:34:55.200 --> 01:34:59.280
Soviet movies had
the biggest influence on me.

01:35:00.480 --> 01:35:04.800
The values there
were very patriotic, I'd say.
990
01:35:04,825 --&gt; 01:35:04,800
were very patriotic, l'd say.

01:35:06.253 --> 01:35:07.813
There was no cynicism.

01:35:09.840 --> 01:35:11.520
Unlike now.

01:35:12.240 --> 01:35:15.360
Dear friends, thank you
for your service to Russia.

01:35:16.800 --> 01:35:20.160
I talk to locals and some think
the Soviet Union will return.

01:35:20.400 --> 01:35:23.160
But it won't! It won't.
996
01:35:23,185 --&gt; 01:35:22,920
KAE

01:35:23.532 --> 01:35:27.612
...to protect our ideals,
culture and national interests...

01:35:28.800 --> 01:35:35.760
Here, I feel disgust, realising that
I don't understand what it's all for.

01:35:36.840 --> 01:35:40.920
...to do everything
for the sake of their beloved country.

01:36:06.600 --> 01:36:08.400
Anastasia, stop filming.

01:36:10.440 --> 01:36:13.440
- Will you marry me?
- What the..?

01:36:13.800 --> 01:36:16.560
Please. I'm at a loss. Fuck!

01:36:16.920 --> 01:36:18.240
Are you serious?

01:36:19.800 --> 01:36:20.640
Come to me, I can't.

01:36:24.720 --> 01:36:26.880
was so nervous!

01:36:28.440 --> 01:36:31.800
Comrade husband, that was unexpected.

01:36:31.800 --> 01:36:34.920
I remember when
we first filmed, and I said...

01:36:35.280 --> 01:36:39.240
I wouldn't have a family,
that I'd devote my life to the army.

01:36:40.440 --> 01:36:44.760
Who knew? He was already
in our unit, sitting in the medic van.

01:36:45.120 --> 01:36:46.200
Who knew?

01:36:47.760 --> 01:36:48.840
Ah, you're here!

01:36:49.200 --> 01:36:53.400
I don't know,
I was so scared, they prepared me.

01:37:01.750 --> 01:37:04.263
I have a different attitude now

01:37:04.288 --> 01:37:07.920
to family, and to having children later.

01:37:11.280 --> 01:37:12.360
It's beautiful.

01:37:13.800 --> 01:37:16.920
My hands are shaking,
why are they are shaking?

01:37:17.880 --> 01:37:19.800
Nightmare!

01:37:20.280 --> 01:37:23.760
So my family is my homeland now.

01:37:51.120 --> 01:37:53.760
We're cleaning up
and going on an offensive.

01:37:55.800 --> 01:37:57.600
Probably tonight.
- How does it feel?
1021
01:37:57,625 --&gt; 01:37:56,880
How does it feel?

01:37:58.920 --> 01:38:02.640
I'm not going, am I crazy?
To die out there.

01:38:03.120 --> 01:38:05.160
I'm not trained for assault.

01:38:05.520 --> 01:38:06.840
I'm a medic anyway.

01:38:06.960 --> 01:38:08.520
They're sending us to die.
- Die where?

01:38:08.640 --> 01:38:09.480
- They're sending us to die.

01:38:09.960 --> 01:38:11.280
Assaulting.

01:38:12.000 --> 01:38:14.520
Klecheevka, in the woods there.

01:38:27.000 --> 01:38:32.400
There's no exact plan on the enemy,
on mine clearance.
1030
01:41:58,345 --&gt; 01:38:31,800
There's no
plan on the enemy,

01:38:32.425 --> 01:38:36.774
They're sending us in with
our eyes closed, like blind kittens.

01:38:37.212 --> 01:38:38.772
We hope for the best.

01:38:39.012 --> 01:38:44.412
- Are you ready to risk your life for...?
- No, I'm not ready to risk my life, I'm not.

01:38:44.520 --> 01:38:46.800
To be honest, no, l'm not ready.

01:38:48.120 --> 01:38:49.320
But...

01:38:49.976 --> 01:38:53.160
I can't refuse, because...

01:38:55.320 --> 01:38:57.240
If I must, I must.

01:38:59.130 --> 01:39:01.213
And you can't argue with that.

01:39:02.760 --> 01:39:05.160
The guys say it's fucked up out there.

01:39:07.560 --> 01:39:08.880
It's targeted.

01:39:09.240 --> 01:39:13.800
When people go in, they get shot at.

01:39:14.520 --> 01:39:16.680
From all sides, both sides.

01:39:28.920 --> 01:39:32.400
People are being killed in droves
and they don't care.

01:39:31.560 --> 01:39:34.560
and they don't care. ,

01:39:51.960 --> 01:39:54.480
Guys, let's take it off.

01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:02.880
Announcement:
breakfast is ready in the kitchen.

01:40:03.000 --> 01:40:06.115
What breakfast? Lunch!
Yes, I apologise, lunch.

01:40:12.960 --> 01:40:16.320
I'm all messed up,
days, breakfasts, dinners...

01:40:22.920 --> 01:40:24.240
So you check...

01:40:24.840 --> 01:40:29.160
For 120 points without a lucky hand
you must collect all cards.

01:40:29.760 --> 01:40:32.520
Fuck, it's hard, I've already forgotten.

01:40:33.840 --> 01:40:36.480
One of these should work for you.

01:40:37.680 --> 01:40:40.440
When you get it, it's a cool process.

01:40:45.120 --> 01:40:49.800
I always thought of Ukrainian people
as brotherly people.

01:40:49.920 --> 01:40:53.520
My roots are in Ukraine,
actually in the West.

01:40:56.520 --> 01:41:00.120
While politicians work out
who has the bigger balls,

01:41:00.480 --> 01:41:02.400
there will be many victims.

01:41:03.120 --> 01:41:05.640
It's time to finish this, enough is enough.

01:41:06.000 --> 01:41:10.320
Let the enemy go home alive
and well to their families, and us too.

01:41:13.680 --> 01:41:18.917
I saw so many guys that weren't
retrieved from near Klecheevka.

01:41:20.173 --> 01:41:22.213
We walked over these corpses.

01:41:24.120 --> 01:41:25.920
There are more bodies here.

01:41:26.280 --> 01:41:28.320
More bodies. They're ours.

01:41:28.920 --> 01:41:30.960
This one. I don't know whose.

01:41:32.400 --> 01:41:33.960
This is ours, with the red.

01:41:34.200 --> 01:41:36.000
He's all black. Fuck.

01:41:37.560 --> 01:41:39.240
They're all ours...

01:41:39.960 --> 01:41:41.640
strewn around.

01:41:43.560 --> 01:41:45.480
He's been here a while.

01:41:46.693 --> 01:41:48.253
That's ours too.

01:41:51.848 --> 01:41:55.345
A God forbid, God forbid.
"I tell you, God forbid!

01:42:02.400 --> 01:42:05.400
We don't say 'no',
but so far, we're all against it.

01:42:10.448 --> 01:42:12.728
For the first time,
I see the guys on edge.

01:42:13.928 --> 01:42:16.328
Almost no one's seen
Ukrainians face-to-face.

01:42:18.477 --> 01:42:22.440
All this time they've been defensive like
WWI soldiers in trenches and dugouts.

01:42:26.400 --> 01:42:29.400
Tomorrow will be their first offensive.

01:42:37.320 --> 01:42:42.379
- I'm going to shoot them in the legs.
Max, enough.

01:42:42.480 --> 01:42:50.640
Brother, you can call me
the last of the blabbermouths.

01:42:51.230 --> 01:42:54.950
Max, stop the hysteria.
- I fucking can't, P.O.

01:42:55.440 --> 01:42:58.320
You get hysterical.
You think no one else gets it?

01:42:58.680 --> 01:42:59.640
Well, fuck!

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:04.920
We're being sent in to slaughter.
You do know that, right?

01:43:05.760 --> 01:43:09.000
Uncle, Uncle... Are you going?

01:43:09.960 --> 01:43:13.560
- Uncle, are you going?
- I'm going, is there a choice?

01:43:52.560 --> 01:43:54.000
We're going, no?

01:43:54.120 --> 01:43:58.560
Why armour? No bullet can get you.
It's for shrapnel, not bullets.

01:43:59.425 --> 01:44:03.245
Cedar, do you have any pain killers?
- Yes.

01:44:08.537 --> 01:44:10.217
You got another tourniquet?

01:44:11.640 --> 01:44:13.713
-Yes.
No, you fucking don't.

01:44:17.255 --> 01:44:20.415
Whoever got in, help the others.

01:44:48.000 --> 01:44:49.560
Victory will be ours!

01:45:04.440 --> 01:45:07.680
Minus One, Minus One,
this is Azimuth. Over.

01:45:09.240 --> 01:45:11.160
Azimuth, receiving.

01:45:12.240 --> 01:45:13.680
Situation report?

01:45:15.480 --> 01:45:18.120
We're moving slowly
No sign of the enemy yet.

01:45:18.240 --> 01:45:18.720
We're moving slowly.

01:45:22.680 --> 01:45:24.120
Did the shelling stop?

01:45:24.840 --> 01:45:27.480
Rain continues, rain continues.

01:45:32.400 --> 01:45:33.960
Minus One, another incoming.

01:45:35.640 --> 01:45:37.680
Minus One, another coming at us.

01:45:42.120 --> 01:45:45.000
A machine gun is firing towards us.

01:45:50.160 --> 01:45:54.720
They've made contact in quadrant 11.

01:45:59.640 --> 01:46:03.840
An APC has been hit
in the woods, left flank.

01:47:13.200 --> 01:47:17.160
Why can't you get in there?
Fucking bitch.

01:47:18.480 --> 01:47:21.480
I'm sending help your way now.

01:47:23.243 --> 01:47:26.280
- Come on, Godspeed!
- Thank you, Comrade Moscow.

01:47:30.960 --> 01:47:34.800
They took your soldier
with a severed leg.

01:47:34.825 --> 01:47:36.000
Blown up by a mine.

01:47:40.320 --> 01:47:42.240
Is Fox in place?

01:47:43.320 --> 01:47:44.760
Fox is 300.

01:47:46.920 --> 01:47:48.720
Are his troops in place?

01:47:50.880 --> 01:47:53.400
Fighters on the left flank rolled back.

01:47:53.760 --> 01:47:56.880
The "dill" [slur for Ukrainians] came in,
they ran from there.

01:47:57.960 --> 01:47:59.640
Did the "dill" take it?

01:48:00.120 --> 01:48:02.400
Anyway, the left flank withdrew.

01:48:03.120 --> 01:48:06.720
The "dill" advanced,
fucking shelled everything.

01:48:11.160 --> 01:48:12.360
Quickly, quickly!

01:48:12.720 --> 01:48:18.000
Rapid assist to evacuate the wounded,
and ready the men to assault.

01:48:20.280 --> 01:48:23.760
No one can move yet.
They're firing cluster bombs.

01:48:27.240 --> 01:48:29.400
I'm hit, I'm hit.

01:48:32.400 --> 01:48:33.840
You're wounded?

01:48:36.600 --> 01:48:40.680
I don't know what's up with my arm.
So far, so good.

01:48:45.000 --> 01:48:48.960
Now it's like a fucking nuclear
bomb was dropped on us.

01:48:49.320 --> 01:48:51.480
It went off pretty bad.

01:48:56.160 --> 01:48:58.800
I need more people here,
a kind of reserve.

01:49:16.440 --> 01:49:18.240
Who's 200?

01:49:23.400 --> 01:49:27.600
Ilgiz and Valera and Tatar.

01:49:32.520 --> 01:49:36.600
- They didn't get Valera out yet?
- Not yet, Valera's still there.

01:49:37.889 --> 01:49:42.142
Did you see Valera or not?
Not yet. They didn't get him out yet.

01:49:42.480 --> 01:49:45.360
They've been carrying wounded all night.

01:49:45.600 --> 01:49:49.560
300s, 200s.
Trucks full of wounded or dead...

01:49:50.400 --> 01:49:51.840
To the hospital?

01:49:53.160 --> 01:49:55.680
They yell at us in the O.R.

01:50:05.400 --> 01:50:06.960
Ilgiz had his legs blown off?

01:50:10.800 --> 01:50:13.560
I don't know what to
write to Ilgiz's mother.
1136
01:50:13,585 --&gt; 01:50:12,000
don't know what to

01:50:16.800 --> 01:50:19.320
What can you write?
You can't make anything up.

01:50:21.600 --> 01:50:24.000
Let Pasha do it, you're the commander.

01:50:24.360 --> 01:50:25.200
I should?

01:50:28.320 --> 01:50:31.800
You should call and talk to her.

01:50:31.825 --> 01:50:32.880
You mean on the phone?

01:50:45.137 --> 01:50:47.663
Commander, take command!

01:50:55.774 --> 01:50:57.213
Wait.

01:51:00.120 --> 01:51:01.680
Valera has three children.

01:51:15.840 --> 01:51:17.400
Cedar's alive.

01:51:24.360 --> 01:51:25.920
Tatar's lying there.

01:51:30.120 --> 01:51:32.160
Cat shot himself.
He shot himself?

01:51:32.760 --> 01:51:34.440
His spine was severed.

01:51:37.320 --> 01:51:40.920
He wouldn't make it, couldn't crawl.

01:51:41.760 --> 01:51:44.400
He was surrounded and shot himself.

01:52:01.680 --> 01:52:03.840
Dudik's legs were broken.

01:52:15.720 --> 01:52:19.035
He said, 'Better you shoot me
than I crawl.'

01:52:20.160 --> 01:52:21.480
He stayed there.

01:52:21.960 --> 01:52:23.760
He's probably 200.

01:52:32.280 --> 01:52:36.840
- With you, I believe in love.
Waiting for you. I love you. -

01:52:37.200 --> 01:52:42.840
- I miss you. May this piece of me
and home be your talisman. -

01:53:24.000 --> 01:53:27.600
The escorting tank was hit
on the first approach.

01:53:30.000 --> 01:53:33.360
Then the enemy artillery began to work.

01:53:35.640 --> 01:53:39.000
We were getting shelled
from three sides.

01:53:40.440 --> 01:53:42.480
We had no support. Nothing.

01:53:44.400 --> 01:53:47.400
I heard Cat's words...
1162
01:53:47,425 --&gt; 01:53:47,280
Theard Cat's words...

01:53:47.520 --> 01:53:49.458
"guys, I'm fucked...

01:53:50.880 --> 01:53:52.800
my legs have failed."

01:53:54.360 --> 01:53:56.640
The front needs to be cleaned.

01:53:59.280 --> 01:54:01.320
Ew, what a smell.

01:54:03.453 --> 01:54:06.498
I took shrapnel in my back.

01:54:14.760 --> 01:54:17.640
A grenade was thrown at me
from a bird [drone].

01:54:15.960 --> 01:54:17.226
from a bird [drone]

01:54:19.680 --> 01:54:23.400
After that it reloaded and
threw a drone grenade at me.

01:54:28.340 --> 01:54:32.540
Just where a guy sat.
The hole is where his legs were.

01:54:40.655 --> 01:54:44.315
pretended to be dead, I won't deny it.

01:54:48.120 --> 01:54:51.120
I heard the "hohols" [slur for Ukrainians]
walk around at night.

01:54:49.920 --> 01:54:52.480
T heard the "hohols" [slur for Ukrainians)

01:54:50.160 --> 01:54:52.720
I heard the "hohols" (slur for Ukrainians]

01:54:50.400 --> 01:54:50.613
Theard the "hohols" [slur for Ukrainians]

01:54:52.920 --> 01:54:54.000
Crawling...

01:54:54.828 --> 01:54:57.072
1 prayed to all the Gods.

01:54:57.960 --> 01:55:00.480
I asked them to keep me alive.

01:55:01.920 --> 01:55:04.200
For strength, to get out of there.

01:55:07.560 --> 01:55:08.880
I got out.

01:55:19.897 --> 01:55:24.480
What can I say? It's a just war after all.

01:55:24.960 --> 01:55:26.400
Very just.

01:55:27.474 --> 01:55:33.234
If we weren't there, there's no telling
what would happen to our Russia.

01:55:33.600 --> 01:55:36.480
The enemy would listen to the West.

01:55:37.800 --> 01:55:42.840
And under this leadership,
they'd besiege our borders.

01:55:43.320 --> 01:55:45.240
And we can't allow that.

01:55:47.640 --> 01:55:48.600
So...

01:55:48.960 --> 01:55:51.240
When did you reach that conclusion?

01:55:53.280 --> 01:55:56.280
I came to that conclusion a while back,

01:55:56.400 --> 01:56:01.800
after being wounded, and now home
in peacetime, on Russian territory...

01:56:03.480 --> 01:56:06.203
think it's right that we're there.

01:56:09.217 --> 01:56:12.480
- But you thought differently before?
- Yes.

01:56:12.840 --> 01:56:14.760
- For world peace

01:56:15.120 --> 01:56:15.840
want peace, for the whole world.

01:56:15.960 --> 01:56:18.360
I want peace, for the whole world.

01:56:20.760 --> 01:56:26.234
You think in a more militant way now,
why is that?

01:56:26.414 --> 01:56:27.589
Why's that?

01:56:29.186 --> 01:56:34.200
Because I'll never forget the faces
of those who were with me at the start.

01:56:35.012 --> 01:56:36.480
I'll never forget.

01:56:38.700 --> 01:56:41.160
They were dying.

01:56:50.280 --> 01:56:52.440
There's this video.

01:56:52.800 --> 01:56:55.320
This is the enemy's Telegram channel.

01:58:01.866 --> 01:58:03.720
I feel guilty.

01:58:05.280 --> 01:58:08.400
Because I couldn't save my friends.

01:59:01.920 --> 01:59:03.360
Oh, my son...

01:59:04.440 --> 01:59:06.960
Oh, how hard it is...

01:59:07.320 --> 01:59:09.960
I raised him, I taught him...

01:59:10.735 --> 01:59:13.680
I had nothing good for myself...

01:59:23.400 --> 01:59:24.960
So we come here.

01:59:26.640 --> 01:59:28.680
Why do we need this glory?

01:59:33.965 --> 01:59:36.845
What will we tell our grandchildren?

01:59:37.800 --> 01:59:39.600
What can I say about him?
Why did he fight?

01:59:42.720 --> 01:59:45.480
Though he said that we'd win,

01:59:45.840 --> 01:59:49.800
he probably didn't understand
who we were fighting, or what for.

01:59:51.960 --> 01:59:55.200
A baffling war, it's baffling for everyone.

01:59:57.480 --> 01:59:58.560
Here, Amin.

01:59:59.520 --> 02:00:01.200
Here is where he lies.

02:00:02.280 --> 02:00:04.320
You know he was so afraid to go there.

02:00:05.640 --> 02:00:08.160
He told everyone,
'I won't come back from there.'

02:00:11.280 --> 02:00:12.600
My darling...

02:00:12.840 --> 02:00:14.520
How I love you.

02:00:15.960 --> 02:00:19.800
You see who came to visit?
Anastasia and your commander.

02:00:23.760 --> 02:00:26.160
Honestly, who really needs this war?

02:00:27.240 --> 02:00:28.440
Maybe someone needs it.

02:00:30.480 --> 02:00:33.360
But not us: wives, mothers and children.

02:00:38.880 --> 02:00:42.960
I give permission for this video
to be used in a documentary.

02:00:43.303 --> 02:00:44.274
I don't mind.

02:00:44.400 --> 02:00:49.680
Let our Russia, and the people,
know what's going on in our world.

02:00:57.845 --> 02:00:59.165
It's so hard...

02:01:03.473 --> 02:01:06.890
All young.
How many are there? How many?

02:01:07.719 --> 02:01:09.831
All so young...

02:01:17.400 --> 02:01:20.160
And he loved all baked foods.

02:01:22.200 --> 02:01:26.760
Let it be there. I'll put it here.

02:01:27.720 --> 02:01:29.160
Eat it, my son.

02:01:30.240 --> 02:01:32.280
Eat, Mom gave it to you.

02:01:46.680 --> 02:01:49.560
I now have many friends here.

02:01:50.640 --> 02:01:53.160
They weren't superhuman, or evil.

02:01:54.720 --> 02:01:57.600
The war machine
dragged many to the front,

02:01:58.200 --> 02:02:02.880
exploiting their sense of patriotism,
friendship and financial need.

02:02:04.560 --> 02:02:07.920
In the end, here lie the ordinary people

02:02:08.520 --> 02:02:12.240
on whose bones big politics is made.

02:02:36.240 --> 02:02:39.000
Hold on, cutie pie.

02:02:46.800 --> 02:02:47.880
Now we'll clean you up.

02:03:00.480 --> 02:03:03.960
Well, what can I do?
You spilled the hot water.

02:03:04.440 --> 02:03:08.400
You didn't have to spill it.
Shush... come on.

02:03:11.400 --> 02:03:13.800
Be patient!

02:03:16.560 --> 02:03:18.000
Cold, huh?

02:03:22.200 --> 02:03:25.800
This whole thing
just came out of the blue.

02:03:28.800 --> 02:03:29.640
And now...

02:03:31.800 --> 02:03:32.760
it's very serious.

02:03:36.480 --> 02:03:39.720
After all, a child is such a responsibility.

02:03:41.640 --> 02:03:44.760
How did you feel when you
found out you were pregnant?

02:03:48.120 --> 02:03:50.760
It's a strange feeling, I don't know.

02:03:52.200 --> 02:03:55.800
It's not joy, it's something strange.

02:03:56.640 --> 02:03:58.200
Fear, sort of...

02:03:58.680 --> 02:04:00.240
So much fear.

02:04:03.600 --> 02:04:05.880
You have to bring him up,

02:04:06.240 --> 02:04:13.320
put all the best into him, so he
grows up to be a decent, good person.

02:04:14.160 --> 02:04:15.720
It's not easy.

02:04:24.240 --> 02:04:26.520
What will you tell him about ...

02:04:27.349 --> 02:04:28.669
The war?
- Yes.

02:04:34.440 --> 02:04:38.880
I don't want to tell my child anything
about it, I don't want to at all.

02:04:44.348 --> 02:04:46.017
Because...

02:04:46.320 --> 02:04:48.840
90% of it is all lies.

02:04:49.800 --> 02:04:51.120
And it's all...

02:04:55.200 --> 02:04:56.760
How shall I put it...

02:04:58.668 --> 02:05:01.548
He wouldn't understand all these things.

02:05:01.920 --> 02:05:07.440
He won't understand that some
people at the top are making money.

02:05:08.640 --> 02:05:10.320
And others die.

02:05:10.553 --> 02:05:14.633
That'll be hard to understand
and explain to a child.

02:05:15.000 --> 02:05:17.520
How do you explain that to a child?

02:05:20.400 --> 02:05:23.280
Teach him the history
of the Russian Empire.

02:05:23.874 --> 02:05:25.794
Which princes ruled.

02:05:26.520 --> 02:05:28.440
Let him learn that...

02:05:29.142 --> 02:05:31.782
But what's going on now...

02:05:33.480 --> 02:05:34.680
It's all very...

02:05:37.920 --> 02:05:41.160
I don't know how I'll explain it all.

